      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(types): remove redundant local aliases",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSmall private type aliases that only rename an existing type add vocabulary without adding narrowing, branding, ownership, or compatibility value. They make signatures harder to trace and obscure the canonical type.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAudit exact identity aliases and remove 20 non-exported, one-use aliases across core and bundled plugins. Each use now names the existing canonical type directly. Exported aliases, documented Plugin SDK names, branded or narrowed types, protocol-state distinctions, generic assertion helpers, and aliases with credible independent evolution value were intentionally excluded. The shipped `ParsedGenerationModelRef` export remains intact.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime or user-visible behavior changes. Maintainers see fewer redundant type names and can trace affected signatures directly to their canonical definitions.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact diff audit: 20 removed `type LocalName = ExistingType` declarations across 20 files; 24 insertions, 55 deletions.\n- Focused behavior proof: 387 tests passed across 17 files and 11 Vitest shards.\n- Follow-up contract proof: 13 tests passed for the restored shipped alias and replacement private status alias.\n- Final `check:changed` passed on Blacksmith Testbox through Crabbox (`tbx_01kwqc1vjyfn010f9kd352xekm`, Actions run `28718244534`).\n- Full build passed on Blacksmith Testbox through Crabbox (`tbx_01kwqbpxth0rshgx8v0vzc9r72`, Actions run `28718096188`).\n- Fresh branch autoreview passed with no accepted/actionable findings.\n",
